{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And when they say to you.</b> He speaks with the disciples." "<b>Who chirp.</b> Similar to speech, and like it: כַּסּוּס עָגוּר כֵּן אֲצְפְצִיף (Isaiah 38:14)." "<b>And who mutter.</b> From the heavy [piel] binyan, added [with hitpa'el form], and the meaning is that they do [this] after muttering." "<b>Should one — a people.</b> This is the answer, the meaning being: should one — this people that seeks its Elohim, in the manner of mocking and ridiculing as [did] Elijah — how can he seek the idols, which are dead, instead of the living?"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {3 "Reading הלה as 'should one'; the phrase בדרך לעג ומהתל כאליהו is rendered as 'in the manner of mocking and ridiculing as [did] Elijah' though the reference is cryptic; possible textual variants in witnesses not checked."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:57.622561188Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}